    "level": "Mandatory",
    "actor": "Marketing authorisation holder",
    "statement": "When the Member State on whose territory the reaction occurred involves the MAH in the follow-up of reports the MAH submitted (e.g. for important missing information for case evaluation or reconciliation, clarification of inconsistent ICSR data, or information for signal validation, safety issue evaluation, PSUR assessment or confirmation of an RMP safety concern), the MAH must carry out that follow-up.",
    "quote": "Furthermore, for reports submitted by a marketing authorisation holder, Member States on whose territory the suspected adverse reaction occurred may involve the marketing authorisation holder in the follow-up of the reports [DIR Art 107a(2)]. The criteria upon which a marketing authorisation holder may be involved include situations where:  important additional information is necessary for case evaluation or reconciliation,  clarifications is needed regarding inconsistent data within ICSRs,  there is a need to obtain further information in the context of the validation of a signal, the evaluation of a safety issue, the assessment of a periodic safety update report, or the confirmation of a safety concern in a risk management plan.",
